WEBVTT

1
00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:22.380
Now that we've described
different types

2
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.050
of options as well
as the roles and

3
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:25.730
responsibilities of buyers and

4
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:27.529
sellers of options contracts,

5
00:00:27.529 --> 00:00:30.260
let's now turn our attention
to how these instruments are

6
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.010
constructed and presented
on a trading platform.

7
00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:37.775
Any IBKR's Trader
Workstations Option Chain,

8
00:00:37.775 --> 00:00:39.290
you'll see a string
of columns that

9
00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.210
provide salient
market information

10
00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:42.890
about call and put options

11
00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:45.530
for particular underlying stock.

12
00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:47.225
Let's say for example,

13
00:00:47.225 --> 00:00:49.415
we've stuck to our movie
theme and we chose

14
00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:55.015
AMC entertainment or ticker
AMC as our underlying stock,

15
00:00:55.015 --> 00:00:57.680
when we do you'll see
these fields of options

16
00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:00.859
related data tied to
the stock populate.

17
00:01:00.859 --> 00:01:03.500
These columns tell you the
prevailing bid and ask

18
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.200
prices for both call
and put contracts,

19
00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.245
as well as their
corresponding contract sizes,

20
00:01:09.245 --> 00:01:12.490
strike prices, and
expiration dates.

21
00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:14.750
The option chain has
several other fields

22
00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.115
you can add to this platform,

23
00:01:16.115 --> 00:01:18.320
but at this stage will
keep the tool as simple as

24
00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.635
possible and start
by exploring these.

25
00:01:21.635 --> 00:01:26.000
Remember, an equity
option is a derivative,

26
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.830
meaning it derives its value

27
00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:29.690
from another financial product,

28
00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:33.565
namely the market value of a
particular underlying stock,

29
00:01:33.565 --> 00:01:36.270
ETF, or similar product,

30
00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:38.965
in this case, AMC stock.

31
00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:41.840
Defined further recall
that a stock option is

32
00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.810
a contract whereby a
buyer and seller agree

33
00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:46.700
to a specified
number of shares for

34
00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:48.320
a particular stock at

35
00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:51.520
a fixed price and over
a defined period.

36
00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.510
Key components of this contract

37
00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:55.745
include the underlying
securities' name,

38
00:01:55.745 --> 00:01:58.265
the month a contract
is due to terminate,

39
00:01:58.265 --> 00:02:01.265
as well as the strike
or exercise price,

40
00:02:01.265 --> 00:02:04.825
and the type of option
whether a call or a put.

41
00:02:04.825 --> 00:02:07.755
In this table, we can
read this option contract

42
00:02:07.755 --> 00:02:10.860
as an AMC September four call.

43
00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.460
For illustration purposes,
let's say you bought one

44
00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:16.490
of these call options
for a premium of $0.11.

45
00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:19.010
You may want to keep in mind
that this premium isn't

46
00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:20.825
a fixed price and it subject to

47
00:02:20.825 --> 00:02:23.374
fluctuation depending
on market dynamics,

48
00:02:23.374 --> 00:02:24.890
including the willingness among

49
00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:26.750
buyers and sellers to act as

50
00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.730
contract owner or writer at

51
00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:31.650
this mutually agreeable
price for that option.

52
00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.970
You may also recall that a
buyer of an options contract

53
00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:38.425
may be referred to as
being long that position.

54
00:02:38.425 --> 00:02:40.220
We can say that as the holder

55
00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.885
of this illustrative contract,

56
00:02:41.885 --> 00:02:44.150
you are long call option,

57
00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:46.610
giving you the right
to buy 100 shares of

58
00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:50.105
an AMC September
four call at $0.11.

59
00:02:50.105 --> 00:02:52.570
Why 100 shares?

60
00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:54.950
As a standard in the
US are typically

61
00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:57.815
100 shares of stock for
each option contract,

62
00:02:57.815 --> 00:03:01.030
this is also considered
a multiplier.

63
00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.455
For example, if I
bought three contracts,

64
00:03:03.455 --> 00:03:04.730
this would mean I'd be long

65
00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:06.740
the AMC September four call at

66
00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:10.250
$0.11 and it would cost
me a premium of $0.33

67
00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.670
to own the contracts or the
right to buy 300 shares at

68
00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:16.175
a fixed price of $4 per share

69
00:03:16.175 --> 00:03:19.295
at or before the
contract expires.

70
00:03:19.295 --> 00:03:21.500
In this case, if the option isn't

71
00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.109
exercised and the
contract expires,

72
00:03:24.109 --> 00:03:25.580
the deal is off the table,

73
00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:27.320
and the option is worthless.

74
00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:29.660
The buyer no longer has
the right to purchase

75
00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:33.380
those 300 shares of AMC
stock at $4 a share,

76
00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:35.570
regardless of where
AMC's market price

77
00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:37.010
may be at the time.

78
00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:40.040
If we look at the strike
price or exercise price

79
00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:43.010
from the perspective of
beholder of a put contract,

80
00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:46.190
then this holder would be
required to sell 300 shares of

81
00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:48.140
AMC stock to the writer or

82
00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:50.845
seller of that contract
for four dollars,

83
00:03:50.845 --> 00:03:54.470
Again regardless of where AMC
stock price in the market

84
00:03:54.470 --> 00:03:58.714
may be at the time if the
buyer's right was exercised.

85
00:03:58.714 --> 00:04:00.905
That's the nature of
the strike price,

86
00:04:00.905 --> 00:04:02.210
which as you may recall,

87
00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:04.520
is that predetermined
fixed price that's

88
00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:07.280
agreed upon in the
options contract.

89
00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.800
It's also the crux of
that critical question

90
00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:11.480
faced by options traders.

91
00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.670
Will the price of the
underlying stock rise or fall?

92
00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:17.840
Strike prices which
are generally set

93
00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:20.020
by the exchange where
the options listed,

94
00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:21.475
are positioned with values

95
00:04:21.475 --> 00:04:24.655
above and below that
stock's market price.

96
00:04:24.655 --> 00:04:26.675
Since those prices fluctuate,

97
00:04:26.675 --> 00:04:28.195
so the strike prices,

98
00:04:28.195 --> 00:04:30.020
with new ones continually created

99
00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:32.165
to reflect those
changes in the market.

100
00:04:32.165 --> 00:04:35.315
But once a contract is in
place, that strike price,

101
00:04:35.315 --> 00:04:37.550
along with the other
components and terms it

102
00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:41.135
contains will be in effect
until its expiration date.

103
00:04:41.135 --> 00:04:43.070
Let's take a look at
the different types of

104
00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:46.150
options and how their
strike prices work.

105
00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:48.320
Call options for example,

106
00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:51.140
with strike prices below the
current trading price of

107
00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:54.860
its underlying shares are
said to be in-the-money.

108
00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.900
However, those with
strike prices above

109
00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.600
the current price of the
underlying shares are said to

110
00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:01.790
be out-of-the-money
and would have

111
00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:04.995
no value if exercised
under those conditions.

112
00:05:04.995 --> 00:05:08.850
The relationship for put
options runs the opposite way.

113
00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.570
Here, strike prices above

114
00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:13.900
the current share price are
said to be in-the-money and

115
00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:15.460
those with strike prices below

116
00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:19.135
the current share price are
said to be out-of-the-money.

117
00:05:19.135 --> 00:05:21.835
Put another way, as a
writer of put options,

118
00:05:21.835 --> 00:05:23.950
you would expect the
underlying share price

119
00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:26.185
to remain above the strike price

120
00:05:26.185 --> 00:05:28.420
over the life of the
contract and you

121
00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:31.535
receive a premium for bearing
the risk that it doesn't.

122
00:05:31.535 --> 00:05:33.900
Turning again to
the option chain,

123
00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:37.195
for this particular class of
call options on AMC stock,

124
00:05:37.195 --> 00:05:39.880
we can see the strike
prices here, above,

125
00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:43.015
and below the market price
for the underlying security.

126
00:05:43.015 --> 00:05:45.025
Now you may have
noticed I mentioned

127
00:05:45.025 --> 00:05:47.460
a particular class of auctions.

128
00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:49.475
When you're trading in
the options market,

129
00:05:49.475 --> 00:05:50.720
you may hear about

130
00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:54.725
different classes of options
or series of options.

131
00:05:54.725 --> 00:05:58.640
If we're talking about all of
the calls on the AMC stock,

132
00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:00.530
for example, we're talking about

133
00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:02.645
the same class of options.

134
00:06:02.645 --> 00:06:04.700
That is one type of option with

135
00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:06.805
the same underlying security.

136
00:06:06.805 --> 00:06:09.630
Whenever we're talking
about all AMC put,

137
00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:11.345
that would be a different class

138
00:06:11.345 --> 00:06:13.565
given it's a different
type of option.

139
00:06:13.565 --> 00:06:15.245
Now, if we were referring to

140
00:06:15.245 --> 00:06:17.375
all the calls on AMC stock that

141
00:06:17.375 --> 00:06:21.050
all had the same expiration
date and exercise price,

142
00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:24.410
we'd be referring to an
option series that has

143
00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:26.120
the same option class with

144
00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:30.470
both the expiry and
exercise price in common.

145
00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:33.110
Now that we've covered
the basic language

146
00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:34.280
of stock options,

147
00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:36.845
what they are and the broad
strokes of how they work,

148
00:06:36.845 --> 00:06:38.120
will dig more deeply into

149
00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:39.950
the new words of these products,

150
00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:42.635
including the benefits and
risks of trading them,

151
00:06:42.635 --> 00:06:44.735
which is the subject
of our next video.

152
00:06:44.735 --> 00:06:47.100
We'll look forward
to seeing you then.